# What this port was made from, and how to notice when it moves.
#
# Source:  dsh-crew 0.6.0  (https://github.com/stuarthu/dsh-crew)
# Commit:  690e291f8444889dbb8b4ed56761d6e3bf28e372
#
# Every line below is the SHA-256 of a dsh-crew file AS COMMITTED at that
# commit — the state this port was made from. To see what has changed since:
#
#   cd ../dsh-crew && sha256sum -c ~/workspace/claude-crew/upstream.sums
#   cd ../dsh-crew && shasum -a 256 -c ~/workspace/claude-crew/upstream.sums   # macOS
#
# A line reported as FAILED means that dsh-crew file changed. The comment above
# it says which claude-crew file to look at, and why. docs/porting.md holds the
# full map and the steps of a port pass.
#
# After carrying a change across, replace that line with the new sum:
#   cd ../dsh-crew && sha256sum roles/pm.md
# and update the Source/Commit lines above when you finish a whole pass.
#
# NOTE: this compares the WORKING TREE of that checkout. Run `git -C ../dsh-crew
# status` first — an uncommitted change is work in progress, not a release.

# roles/pm.md  ->  skills/team-lane/SKILL.md
#     Step 0, the PM rules, the roster and limits, then the 14 steps — all in the skill.
